# Third-party benchmark data -- MemoryAgentBench ships its own terms; fetch it with the
# curl command in README.md rather than redistributing it here.
data/*.parquet

# Raw per-query calibration dumps (~1.5MB). Regenerate with
# `python -m memore.bench.calibrate --configs all --reingest`; the conclusions they
# support are summarised in RESULTS.md §5 and §9.
data/results/calibration.json
data/results/calibration_gate.json
data/results/calib_nosubj.json
data/results/calib_subjcheck.json
data/results/w4/control.json
data/results/w4/dump.json

# ...but data/results/w4/gate_features.csv IS committed. It is B1's deliverable rather
# than a byproduct: one row per query per regime, joinable to the labels, and the point of
# W4 is that someone can start from it without re-running anything. RESULTS.md §28.

